expression: "help(&[\"snapshot\", \"save\", \"--help\"])"
---
Capture the state of a running instance into a `.tensor-wasm` file via the API

Usage: tensor-wasm snapshot save [OPTIONS] --instance <INSTANCE> --output <OUTPUT> --server <SERVER>

Options:
      --instance <INSTANCE>  Identifier of the running instance to snapshot
      --tenant <TENANT>      Tenant id to advertise on outbound API requests via `X-TensorWasm-Tenant`. Zero (the default) suppresses the header for backwards compatibility [default: 0]
      --output <OUTPUT>      Output path for the resulting `.tensor-wasm` archive
      --server <SERVER>      Base URL of the target TensorWasm server (e.g. `http://localhost:8080`)
  -h, --help                 Print help
